    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `extract_layout.py` script that extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Textract service. Amazon Textract is a machine learning service that automatically extracts text, handwriting, and data from scanned documents. It will be identifiable in the code through the use of the `boto3` library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, and the specific service client for Textract. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789888113312,
          "start": 1789888110697
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bda52069001ZYfs87J9QKWtnl",
      "message_id": "msg_0bda51be4001M05Ne0QIhfxPSC",
      "session_id": "ses_f425ae42cffedFF9HkCUmYm5X7",
      "time_created": 1789888110697,
      "time_updated": 1789888113312
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_sGqYf5VRXBJkwHJVvgroxc",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef extract_layout(document_path):\n    textract_client = boto3.client('textract')\n\n    with open(document_path, 'rb') as document:\n        image_bytes = document.read()\n\n    response = textract_client.detect_document_text(\n        Document={'Bytes': image_bytes}\n    )\n\n    blocks = response['Blocks']\n    lines = [block for block in blocks if block['BlockType'] == 'LINE']\n    tables = [block for block in blocks if block['BlockType'] == 'TABLE']\n\n    return {\n        'lines': lines,\n        'tables': tables\n    }\n\n# Example usage:\n# print(extract_layout('path_to_your_document.png'))",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-nawnjzkj/extract_layout.py"
          },
